    {
      "n": 3,
      "title": "Genetic Drift & Gene Flow",
      "competency": "STEM_BIO11/12-IIIC-g-9",
      "content": "<h3>🎯 Learning Objectives</h3><ul><li>Define genetic drift.</li><li>Differentiate bottleneck and founder effects.</li><li>Define gene flow.</li><li>Compare drift and selection.</li></ul><h3>🔑 Key Concepts</h3><ul><li><strong>Genetic drift</strong> — random change in allele frequencies.</li><li><strong>Bottleneck effect</strong> — sharp reduction in population size.</li><li><strong>Founder effect</strong> — new population from a small group.</li><li><strong>Gene flow</strong> — movement of alleles between populations.</li></ul><h3>📚 Lesson Content</h3><h4>A. Genetic Drift</h4><ul><li>Random</li><li>More pronounced in small populations</li><li>Can eliminate beneficial alleles</li></ul><h4>B. Bottleneck vs Founder</h4><table><thead><tr><th>Effect</th><th>Cause</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Bottleneck</td><td>Population crash (disaster, disease)</td></tr><tr><td>Founder</td><td>Small group colonizes new area</td></tr></tbody></table><h4>C. Gene Flow</h4><ul><li>Moves alleles between populations</li><li>Reduces differences between populations</li><li>Can introduce new alleles</li></ul>",
      "activity1": {
        "timeLimit": 90,
        "badgeId": "drift-master",
        "badgeName": "Drift Master",
        "badgeIcon": "🌊",
        "pairs": [
          { "key": "drift", "left": "Genetic drift", "right": "Random allele frequency change" },
