    {
      "n": 4,
      "title": "Mutation & Recombination",
      "competency": "STEM_BIO11/12-IIIC-g-9",
      "content": "<h3>🎯 Learning Objectives</h3><ul><li>Explain mutation as a source of variation.</li><li>Describe recombination's role.</li><li>Distinguish mutation from selection.</li><li>Explain why variation is essential for evolution.</li></ul><h3>🔑 Key Concepts</h3><ul><li><strong>Mutation</strong> — change in DNA; source of new alleles.</li><li><strong>Recombination</strong> — shuffling of alleles during meiosis.</li><li><strong>Variation</strong> — raw material for evolution.</li></ul><h3>📚 Lesson Content</h3><h4>A. Mutation</h4><ul><li>Only source of NEW alleles</li><li>Random with respect to fitness</li><li>Can be beneficial, neutral, or harmful</li></ul><h4>B. Recombination</h4><ul><li>Crossing over during Prophase I</li><li>Independent assortment</li><li>Shuffles existing alleles into new combinations</li></ul><h4>C. Variation & Evolution</h4><ul><li>Without variation, no evolution by selection</li><li>Mutation + recombination + sexual reproduction → diversity</li></ul>",
      "activity1": {
        "timeLimit": 90,
